    "knowledge_point": "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Polynomial",
    "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13928579/assets/fb4959f437e11b767be136a2a024260d45ed29805cd57b1832d74d7cc2da11c1.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $y=P(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n- The degree of $P(x)$ is odd.\n- The coefficient of the leading term is negative.",
    "worked_solution": "The end behavior of $P(x)$ is\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty ,$ and\n\n- $P(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nConsequently, \n\n- the degree of $P(x)$ is even, and\n\n- the leading coefficient of $P(x)$ is negative.\n\nTherefore, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.",
